Ladybird resolves an extension directory to its real, absolute path
before comparing or storing it. Blink makes the path absolute too, with
MakeAbsoluteFilePath() in UnpackedInstaller::LoadFromCommandLine();
Gecko’s temporary add-on install takes an nsIFile, which rejects a
relative path in InitWithNativePath(); and WebKit keeps a file resource
URL, which is always absolute.

A reload or a re-enable gives the extension a new revision, so the
contexts of the old instance lose their authority. Blink tears them
down in Dispatcher::UnloadExtension(), through ScriptContextSet::
OnExtensionUnloaded(), and WebKit in WebExtensionContext::unload().
Gecko’s ContentScriptContextChild::close() unloads the APIs and nukes
the content script’s sandbox.
